{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44116078",
      "title": "Using Custom DI Tokens & Providers",
      "lectureOrder": 188,
      "videoOrder": 180,
      "sourceHash": "79645ddee1f3c3b599a55451c5b927f0f94b1801a977f48977b79ae1597eeaad",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.589,
          "end": 2.4,
          "en": "Now that we learned",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.4,
          "end": 4.71,
          "en": "how to inject services into services,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 4.71,
          "end": 7.32,
          "en": "and we had a look at this injector tree",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 7.32,
          "end": 9.42,
          "en": "in the developer tools,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 9.42,
          "end": 10.77,
          "en": "I wanna dive a bit deeper",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 10.77,
          "end": 15.24,
          "en": "into the dependency injection mechanism offered by Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 15.24,
          "end": 18.3,
          "en": "And I wanna start by diving a bit deeper",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 18.3,
          "end": 22.86,
          "en": "into how services or injectable values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 22.86,
          "end": 27.12,
          "en": "in general, are registered with Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.12,
          "end": 29.88,
          "en": "And I already showed you different places",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.88,
          "end": 32.85,
          "en": "where you can register services, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.85,
          "end": 35.7,
          "en": "And I mentioned that this @Injectable approach,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 35.7,
          "end": 39.51,
          "en": "is the most common way of registering it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 39.51,
          "end": 41.79,
          "en": "But I wanna show you what's happening behind the scenes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 41.79,
          "end": 44.553,
          "en": "in the end when you register a service.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 45.63,
          "end": 48.54,
          "en": "And for that, I'll comment out @Injectable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 48.54,
          "end": 50.673,
          "en": "and go back to the main TS file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 51.54,
          "end": 56.34,
          "en": "And there, I'll bring back this code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 56.34,
          "end": 59.85,
          "en": "where I provide the TasksService like this instead,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 59.85,
          "end": 63.33,
          "en": "which also works as you saw before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 63.33,
          "end": 67.29,
          "en": "I got no error here when switching to that code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 67.29,
          "end": 70.5,
          "en": "But this code here is actually a shortcut",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 70.5,
          "end": 75.39,
          "en": "for an alternative way of registering your service.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 75.39,
          "end": 78.3,
          "en": "And you would typically use that shortcut,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 78.3,
          "end": 81.99,
          "en": "don't get me wrong, but I find it important to understand",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 81.99,
          "end": 83.67,
          "en": "what's happening behind the scenes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 83.67,
          "end": 86.52,
          "en": "Because what is happening behind the scenes is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 86.52,
          "end": 90.6,
          "en": "that Angular creates a provider object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 90.6,
          "end": 93.513,
          "en": "which is registered with the providers here in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 94.5,
          "end": 99.42,
          "en": "And that's an object which has a provide property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 99.42,
          "end": 103.59,
          "en": "And then one of these other use properties here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 103.59,
          "end": 105.43299999999999,
          "en": "like useClass, useExisting,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 105.43299999999999,
          "end": 107.88300000000001,
          "en": "useFactory or useValue.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 109.2,
          "end": 112.35,
          "en": "And the idea behind this provide property is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 112.35,
          "end": 116.85,
          "en": "that it registers the so-called injection token",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 116.85,
          "end": 121.08,
          "en": "of the injectable thing you are trying to register,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 121.08,
          "end": 123.87,
          "en": "so of the service, you are trying to register,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 123.87,
          "end": 125.79,
          "en": "in this case here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 125.79,
          "end": 129.45,
          "en": "And the idea behind an injection token is simply",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 129.45,
          "end": 133.923,
          "en": "that it acts as the identifier of the injectable thing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 135.27,
          "end": 136.38,
          "en": "Now, by default,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 136.38,
          "end": 138.21,
          "en": "when you use that shortcut,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 138.21,
          "end": 142.65,
          "en": "the name of the service class is the token.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 142.65,
          "end": 145.82999999999998,
          "en": "That's why in the places where you need it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 145.82999999999998,
          "end": 148.41,
          "en": "in the tasks list component, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 148.41,
          "end": 153.24,
          "en": "you can use it as a token, as an identifier passed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 153.24,
          "end": 156.84300000000002,
          "en": "to the inject function or in the constructor function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 157.86,
          "end": 160.95,
          "en": "So that is the identifier that tells Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 160.95,
          "end": 163.315,
          "en": "what you wanna inject,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 163.315,
          "end": 167.91,
          "en": "but you could also register your own token instead.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 167.91,
          "end": 170.01,
          "en": "And you can create such a token,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 170.01,
          "end": 173.973,
          "en": "let's say, the tasks service token,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 175.14,
          "end": 176.88,
          "en": "by constructing a new value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 176.88,
          "end": 180.513,
          "en": "of type injection token like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 181.89,
          "end": 185.76,
          "en": "And that is something that's imported from @angular/core,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 185.76,
          "end": 188.343,
          "en": "this injection token thing here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 189.33,
          "end": 192.6,
          "en": "Now, injection token then needs a description,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 192.6,
          "end": 194.88,
          "en": "which in the end, is used internally",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 194.88,
          "end": 197.55,
          "en": "and for debugging purposes, which is up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 197.55,
          "end": 201.54,
          "en": "And here, I'll name it tasks-service-token like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 201.54,
          "end": 202.95,
          "en": "But again, this is up to you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 202.95,
          "end": 205.32,
          "en": "it's just some identifier that can help",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 205.32,
          "end": 208.233,
          "en": "with debugging error messages, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 209.79,
          "end": 212.01,
          "en": "But now that we got such a token here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 212.01,
          "end": 216.63,
          "en": "we can go back to this manual configuration mode here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 216.63,
          "end": 219.31,
          "en": "and then set this TasksServiceToken",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 220.68,
          "end": 222.903,
          "en": "as a value for the provide property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 224.31,
          "end": 228.09300000000002,
          "en": "Now, we just also need to add one of these used properties.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 229.02,
          "end": 233.46,
          "en": "And if we wanna make a class injectable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 233.46,
          "end": 234.99,
          "en": "as it's the case here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 234.99,
          "end": 238.77,
          "en": "where this task service class should be injectable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 238.77,
          "end": 240.873,
          "en": "you wanna use useClass here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 241.8,
          "end": 244.563,
          "en": "and then use TasksService like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 245.85,
          "end": 248.22,
          "en": "And that would be the long form",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 248.22,
          "end": 250.47,
          "en": "with a custom injection token",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 250.47,
          "end": 254.133,
          "en": "of providing your tasks service to the application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 255.72,
          "end": 258,
          "en": "Now, if you wanted to inject it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 258,
          "end": 260.163,
          "en": "you would have to use your own token,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 261.12,
          "end": 262.62,
          "en": "otherwise you'll get an error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 262.62,
          "end": 264.45,
          "en": "that the dependency isn't found,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 264.45,
          "end": 266.79,
          "en": "because in the code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 266.79,
          "end": 269.34,
          "en": "in the tasks list component, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 269.34,
          "end": 272.22,
          "en": "we're still looking for a value with an injection token",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 272.22,
          "end": 274.17,
          "en": "of tasks service.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 274.17,
          "end": 277.44,
          "en": "And this injection token isn't registered anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 277.44,
          "end": 281.763,
          "en": "Instead, this is my injection token now, TasksServiceToken.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 283.71,
          "end": 286.29,
          "en": "So it's that token that now needs to be used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 286.29,
          "end": 288.78,
          "en": "in other places of the app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 288.78,
          "end": 291.09000000000003,
          "en": "and therefore I'll export it here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 291.09000000000003,
          "end": 293.61,
          "en": "and you might wanna store it in a separate file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 293.61,
          "end": 297.21,
          "en": "Here, I'll just leave it in this file and I'll export it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 297.21,
          "end": 301.38,
          "en": "And in the tasks list component, I now have to import",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 301.38,
          "end": 304.893,
          "en": "and use this tasks service token like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 308.37,
          "end": 310.23,
          "en": "with that TypeScript complaints",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 310.23,
          "end": 313.95,
          "en": "because it doesn't understand which kind of value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 313.95,
          "end": 316.83,
          "en": "will be provided through that token.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 316.83,
          "end": 320.91,
          "en": "It's an unknown value because indeed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 320.91,
          "end": 324.15,
          "en": "when we set up that token, we don't tell TypeScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 324.15,
          "end": 326.883,
          "en": "which kind of value will be provided through it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 328.17,
          "end": 331.56,
          "en": "That's why injection token is a generic class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 331.56,
          "end": 333.48,
          "en": "and you can use angle brackets",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 333.48,
          "end": 336.96,
          "en": "to add extra type information to it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 336.96,
          "end": 339.57,
          "en": "In this case, you would tell TypeScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 339.57,
          "end": 344.4,
          "en": "which kind of value will be provided through that token.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 344.4,
          "end": 345.24,
          "en": "And in that case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 345.24,
          "end": 348.45,
          "en": "that will be a value of type TasksService,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 348.45,
          "end": 350.85,
          "en": "since we're providing an instance of this class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 352.40999999999997,
          "end": 354.513,
          "en": "With this annotation added here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 355.53,
          "end": 357.483,
          "en": "the errors here would go away.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 359.07,
          "end": 363.72,
          "en": "Now the task item component needs a similar treatment",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 363.72,
          "end": 366.39,
          "en": "because they are injecting the tasks service,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 366.39,
          "end": 367.62,
          "en": "like this won't work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 367.62,
          "end": 372.003,
          "en": "Instead it's now the TasksServiceToken that's needed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 374.4,
          "end": 378.873,
          "en": "And the new task component also needs an adjustment.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 379.74,
          "end": 381.513,
          "en": "Here, I'm using the constructor,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 382.56,
          "end": 385.51,
          "en": "and therefore here we also wanna import",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 391.59,
          "end": 393.6,
          "en": "from this main file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 393.6,
          "end": 395.343,
          "en": "and import this TasksServiceToken.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 397.11,
          "end": 400.98,
          "en": "And we could try to use that as a value here now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 400.98,
          "end": 404.01,
          "en": "But as you see, this would now give us an error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 404.01,
          "end": 407.04,
          "en": "because indeed, when using a custom token,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 407.04,
          "end": 410.52,
          "en": "you can't use it as a type definition like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 410.52,
          "end": 414.21,
          "en": "Instead, now you need to add a special decorator",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 414.21,
          "end": 417.3,
          "en": "in front of your parameter here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 417.3,
          "end": 420.483,
          "en": "when using this constructor approach for injecting,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 421.41,
          "end": 424.833,
          "en": "and it's the inject decorator that you need to use here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 425.76,
          "end": 429.18,
          "en": "which is provided by Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 429.18,
          "end": 432.63,
          "en": "So not the inject function with a lowercase eye,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 432.63,
          "end": 435.513,
          "en": "but the inject decorator with an uppercase eye.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 436.77,
          "end": 439.32,
          "en": "And then you can pass your tasks service token",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 439.32,
          "end": 440.763,
          "en": "as a value to that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 441.66,
          "end": 445.08,
          "en": "We now need to set the type of value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 445.08,
          "end": 447.303,
          "en": "we'll get here for the TasksService,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 448.59,
          "end": 449.423,
          "en": "and that, of course,",
          "zh": ""
